Add a wasm-max-memory build option that sets the module's maximum linear
memory. wasm2go turns that maximum into a constant, and vibepit uses it
to cap each emulator instance.

Upstream: not yet proposed.

diff --git a/src/build/GhosttyLibVt.zig b/src/build/GhosttyLibVt.zig
index a200209af..ab837467b 100644
--- a/src/build/GhosttyLibVt.zig
+++ b/src/build/GhosttyLibVt.zig
@@ -65,6 +65,13 @@ pub fn initWasm(
     // comment but lets do 128KB to be safe. We can lower later.
     exe.stack_size = 128 * 1024;
 
+    // Linear memory can grow to 4 GiB unless an embedder caps it here.
+    if (b.option(
+        u64,
+        "wasm-max-memory",
+        "Maximum linear memory of the wasm module in bytes, a multiple of 64 KiB",
+    )) |max| exe.max_memory = max;
+
     // Zig's WASM linker doesn't support --growable-table, so the table
     // is emitted with max == min and can't be grown from JS. Run a
     // small Zig build tool that patches the binary's table section to
